						<!-- Presets Tab Content -->
						<div id="panel-presets" class="hidden p-[16px] mobile:p-5">
							<label id="preset-label" class="block text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.4px] text-ink-subtle mb-2">
								Common Compounds
							</label>
							<!--
								Custom listbox replacing the native <select>. On mobile a native
								<select> with <optgroup>s hands off to the OS's own picker (wheel
								or full-screen overlay depending on platform), which can't be
								restyled and doesn't respect the page's width — this reimplements
								the same "pick one grouped value" interaction as an in-page
								combobox, per the ARIA APG "Collapsible Dropdown Listbox"
								(select-only combobox) pattern: focus stays on the trigger the
								whole time, aria-activedescendant tracks the highlighted option
								instead of DOM focus moving into the listbox.

								Selecting an option (click, or Enter/Space while highlighted)
