								</button>
								<!-- Same glyph/spec as #browse-chevron: 6x10.5 viewBox, 1.5px
								     stroke, round caps/joins — rotated 90° permanently, since
								     this chevron never animates (unlike #browse-chevron). -->
								<svg class="pointer-events-none absolute right-3.5 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 rotate-90 text-ink-muted" width="6" height="10.5" viewBox="0 0 6 10.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
									<path d="M0.75 9.75L5.25 5.25L0.75 0.75" />
								</svg>
								<!-- Populated by JS from PRESETS (src/utils/browseElements.ts) —
								     see the note above the script's Presets section for why the
								     data isn't duplicated here.

								     position:fixed, not absolute: #browse-panel (an ancestor,
								     several levels up) carries overflow-hidden to keep its own
								     rounded corners clean, and an absolutely-positioned popup's
								     containing block (this element's nearest positioned ancestor,
								     the .relative wrapper above) still sits *inside* that clipping
								     box — so `absolute` got clipped flush with #browse-panel's
								     bottom edge, cutting the list off after ~1 row. Fixed
								     positioning's containing block is the viewport itself (no
								     ancestor here sets transform/filter/perspective/contain, any
								     of which would pull it back into a local containing block), so
								     it escapes that clip entirely. top/left/width are computed from
								     #preset-trigger's own bounding rect in JS on open, since fixed
								     has no positioned-ancestor offset to lean on the way absolute
								     did. -->
								<div
									id="preset-listbox"
									role="listbox"
									aria-labelledby="preset-label"
									tabindex="-1"
									class="hidden fixed z-20 max-h-72 overflow-y-auto bg-surface-1 inset-ring-1 inset-ring-hairline rounded-[8px] py-1"
